cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Alloy in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "Alloy physics engine"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "Argon Robotics"
abstract: >-
  Alloy is a multi-material, parallel physics engine for robot learning, built on Newton, MuJoCo Warp and Warp:
  rigid robots, cloth, liquids, sand and soft bodies in one scene, stepped together in parallel worlds on a GPU or on
  a CPU. The package is alloy-engine; the import is alloy.
license: Apache-2.0
url: "https://alloy.argonrobotics.ai"
repository-code: "https://github.com/argonrobotics-ai/alloy"
keywords:
  - physics engine
  - robotics
  - robot learning
  - simulation
  - cloth
  - liquid
  - soft body
  - reinforcement learning
  - MuJoCo
  - Newton
  - Warp
  - sim-to-real
